            "type": "string",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          },
          "labels": {
            "type": [
              "set",
              "string"
            ],
            "description": "Labels to attach to the object",
            "description_kind": "markdown",
            "optional": true
          },
          "name": {
            "type": "string",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          },
          "required_type": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The data type the entity is encoded as. If set, tables' entity columns must be of this type. One of string, integer, long, or binary",
            "description_kind": "markdown",
            "optional": true
          }
        },
        "block_types": {
          "attribute": {
            "nesting_mode": "set",
            "block": {
              "attributes": {
                "key": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description_kind": "plain",
                  "required": true
                },
                "value": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description_kind": "plain",
                  "optional": true
                }
              },
              "description": "Attributes (key value pairs) to attach to the object",
              "description_kind": "markdown"
            }
          }
        },
        "description": "# Entities\n\nAn Entity is an item in the business domain. Common examples of Entities are:\n\n- Customers\n- Accounts\n- Products\n- Orders\n\nAnything that has a unique identifier and would be useful to report or predict on could be an Entity.\n\nIn a relational database, the identifiers for Entities will often be used for primary keys.\n\nTables need to specify one or more columns with entity identifiers in order to be used for Feature definitions.\n\nFeatures will be generated for a specific Entity. This means the aggregation will be grouped by each Entity identitifer.\n",
        "description_kind": "markdown"
      }
    },
    "anaml_entity_mapping": {
      "version": 0,
      "block": {
        "attributes": {
          "from": {
            "type": "string",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          },
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          },
          "mapping": {
            "type": "string",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          },
          "to": {
            "type": "string",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          }
        },
        "block_types": {
          "one_to_many": {
            "nesting_mode": "list",
            "block": {
              "description": "The mapping feature produces an array of keys which are related.",
              "description_kind": "markdown"
            },
            "max_items": 1
          },
          "one_to_one": {
            "nesting_mode": "list",
            "block": {
              "description": "The mapping feature produce a single key (or null), which is related.",
              "description_kind": "markdown"
            },
            "max_items": 1
          }
        },
        "description": "# Entity Mappings\n\nAn Entity Mapping is a relationship between one or more Entities so that features can\nautomatically be aggregated at different levels without defining the Feature multiple times.\n\nEach Entity Mapping specifies:\n\n- From Entity - The Entity that the Feature is initially defined on\n- To Entity - The Entity that can be converted to\n- Mapping Feature - A Feature that is defined on the *from* Entity and has a value of the *to* Entity.\n\nFor example, given a customer and account Entities where each customer has multiple accounts\nyou could define an Entity Mapping from Account to Customer:\n\n- From Entity = Account\n- To Entity = Customer\n- Mapping Feature = Last Customer Id for each Account Id\n",
        "description_kind": "markdown"
      }
    },
