                  "description_kind": "plain",
                  "required": true
                },
                "value": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description_kind": "plain",
                  "optional": true
                }
              },
              "description": "Attributes (key value pairs) to attach to the object",
              "description_kind": "markdown"
            }
          }
        },
        "description": "# Entity Populations\n\nAn Entity Population allows for the specification of entities and dates to run feature generation for.\nThis is used for feature \"time travel\", as well as generating data for a reduced set of entities.\n\nAn entity population is specified from a table or set of tables using SQL. The entity population must\nreturn a two column dataset, the first of which is named for the selected entity's output column; and\nthe second of which is named \"date\".\n",
        "description_kind": "markdown"
      }
    },
